{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Sign","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Cycle.Type","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.deg_three_six_branch_points_not_S3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.deg_three_six_branch_points_not_S3","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L173-L183","doc":"**The conclusion for the colour leg.**  A degree-3 covering whose every\nbranch point is totally ramified has 3-cycle monodromy at each, so its monodromy\ngroup is generated by even permutations and is **not** `S₃`.\n\nThis contradicts `brings-qou-4tuple.md:15`, which derives the `SO(3)` holonomy\nrepresentation from *\"the `S₃` permutation of the three sheets\"* in the same\nsentence that fixes the degree at 3 with six branch points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.generated_by_three_cycles_ne_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.generated_by_three_cycles_ne_top","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L151-L171","doc":"**The monodromy group generated by 3-cycles is proper.**  Every generator is\neven, so every element of the generated subgroup is even; `S₃` contains odd\npermutations, so the subgroup is not all of `S₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.sign_of_isThreeCycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.sign_of_isThreeCycle","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L146-L149","doc":"A 3-cycle in `S₃` is an even permutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.no_simple_branch_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.no_simple_branch_point","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L137-L140","doc":"Restated: if `k` of the six branch points were only simply ramified\n(contributing 1 rather than 2), the total would fall short of 12. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.six_points_forces_total_ramification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.six_points_forces_total_ramification","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L129-L135","doc":"**Twelve is exactly the budget, so the bound is saturated.**  At genus 4,\ndegree 3 and exactly six branch points, every branch point must be *totally*\nramified — fibre profile `(3)`, monodromy a 3-cycle.  There is no slack: one\nbranch point of profile `(2,1)` would contribute 1 instead of 2 and the total\ncould not reach 12. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.six_points_budget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.six_points_budget","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L126-L127","doc":"Six branch points of a degree-3 map contribute at most `6 · 2 = 12`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.fibreRamificationBound_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.fibreRamificationBound_three","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.fibreRamificationBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.fibreRamificationBound","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L119-L122","doc":"A single fibre of a degree-`d` map contributes at most `d − 1` to the total\nramification: the fibre has at most `d` preimages and `Σ(eᵢ − 1) = d − #preimages`,\nmaximised when the fibre is a single totally-ramified point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.deg_three_and_R_fourteen_incompatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.deg_three_and_R_fourteen_incompatible","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L115-L117","doc":"The two stated data cannot describe a single map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.ramification_fourteen_forces_deg_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.ramification_fourteen_forces_deg_four","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L109-L113","doc":"`R = 14` at genus 4 forces degree 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.ramification_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.ramification_inj","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L101-L107","doc":"**The total ramification determines the degree.**  So `R = 14` is compatible\nwith one degree only, and the two blocks describe one map only if their degrees\nagree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.bring_deg_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.bring_deg_three","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L98-L99","doc":"Bring's surface at the 4-tuple block's degree: `R = 12`, **not** 14. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.bring_deg_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.bring_deg_four","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L95-L96","doc":"Bring's surface at the verification block's degree: `R = 14`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.ramification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.CoveringDegreeRamification.ramification","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/CoveringDegreeRamification.lean#L87-L93","doc":"Total ramification of a degree-`d` branched covering of `ℙ¹` by a genus-`g`\ncurve, as forced by Riemann–Hurwitz: `2g − 2 = d·(2·0 − 2) + R`, so\n`R = 2g − 2 + 2d`.\n\nThis is a **definition encoding** Riemann–Hurwitz for a `ℙ¹` target, not a proof\nof it — Mathlib has no branched-covering API. ","signatureChunk":0}]}